<p>Palestinians voted in municipal elections across the Israeli-occupied West Bank and in Deir el-Balah in central Gaza, marking the first local vote since the Gaza war began and the first election in part of Gaza in more than two decades. The vote focused on local councils rather than national leadership, and it unfolded in a tense environment shaped by war damage in Gaza, displacement, and ongoing insecurity in the West Bank. Even so, the election gave many voters a rare chance to focus on practical community needs such as water, roads, and municipal services. Some residents and officials described the day as an important exercise in local democracy. Turnout was lower than in previous West Bank municipal elections, reaching 40.62% in the West Bank and 21.2% in Deir el-Balah by closing time, according to the Central Elections Commission, underscoring both voter fatigue and the difficulty of casting ballots during conflict.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/vYqdWplhdRxakbMg6Ct_oNAJn6rIDghnmEILhkpGcsNg9kqO6BiCHQGfgmzp0oOeeADgnTa-fKHcTd0T3aZ7OzXywSMgGSyupdkW-tkqe65e' alt='Two women register to vote at a polling station near Jenin, in the Israeli-occupied West Bank.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Voter base: Nearly 1.5 million people were registered to vote in the West Bank and about 70,000 in the Deir el-Balah area, according to the Ramallah-based Central Elections Commission.</li><li>Diplomat presence: Foreign diplomats observed the voting process in the West Bank as polling stations saw a steady flow of voters throughout the day.</li><li>Women surge: Dawn reported a notable late surge of women voters in Jericho before West Bank polling closed at 7pm local time.</li><li>Past comparison: Turnout in the West Bank trailed the 53.7% recorded in the previous municipal elections in March 2022.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Mahmud Abbas: After voting in Al-Bireh, the Palestinian president called the election a democratic exercise despite local and international challenges. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995095/low-turnout-as-palestinians-vote-in-first-elections-since-start-of-gaza-conflict'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Manar Salman: The English teacher in Jericho said she wanted local representatives who could improve water supply and repair streets, while noting that the occupation limits what municipalities can do. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995095/low-turnout-as-palestinians-vote-in-first-elections-since-start-of-gaza-conflict'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Deir el-Balah residents: Al Jazeera described a mood of joy and a desire for change among residents voting in Deir el-Balah despite destruction and displacement. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/4/25/joy-and-desire-for-change-as-gazas-deir-el-balah-holds-elections'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn4vej3x0wxo'>Palestinians in West Bank and some in Gaza vote in local elections</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/4/25/joy-and-desire-for-change-as-gazas-deir-el-balah-holds-elections'>Joy and desire for change as Gaza’s Deir el-Balah holds elections</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/25/palestinians-vote-in-west-bank-and-central-gaza-municipal-elections-the-first-since-war-st'>Palestinians vote in West Bank and central Gaza municipal elections, the first since war started</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/palestinians-vote-in-municipal-elections-in-gaza-west-bank/a-76930149'>Palestinians vote in municipal elections in Gaza, West Bank</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/palestinians-vote-in-the-first-gaza-elections-held-in-more-than-20-years'>Palestinians vote in the first Gaza elections held in more than 20 years</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995095/low-turnout-as-palestinians-vote-in-first-elections-since-start-of-gaza-conflict'>Low turnout as Palestinians vote in first elections since start of Gaza conflict</a> - dawn.com</li></ul>